Z||000022||Mach10||09-08-2001||01:31 PM||||That doesn't sound AT ALL like rod-knock. Rod knock, in my experience, is a thud-thud noise that sounds like someone's banging on the block with a hammer. Gets louder when you acellerate, and almost disappears as it's coasting down. Sounds to me like you are running rich and it's bacfiring. Check/replace your timing, plugs, wires, and 0-2 sensor. Other than that, it's an exhaust system problem. Maybe a leak, cracked manifold, rusted-through muffler etc. Don't get all scared until you know for sure what the problem is. Use a length of rubber hose, one end in your ear, to find the source of the noise. Start planning the fix WHEN you find out what's wrong...||||reg||3
