Z||000025||Mach10||09-08-2001||02:30 PM||||That's not a rod, that's a Fuel/spark problem, both of which would cause that popping. Pull codes, me boyo.||||reg||7
Z||000026||sqoach||09-08-2001||02:34 PM||||Sounds like it has something to do with your exhaust system. And as Mach10 stated, don't get too worked up over it. Might not be as bad as you think.<P>And I sent you an e-mail.||||reg||1
Z||000027||JamesWM83||09-09-2001||12:23 AM||||That's not a rod. I can guarantee that. I had a rod go out in my 86 SE. A rod knockin is a loud smashing of metal sound. You have a problem somewhere in your electrical ignition system. Sounds like you need to get a new coil, new wires, and new plugs, and then see if it still does it. If it does it's prolly just a leak in one of the manifolds. Hope that helps. Don't worry about replacin the engine. Later<P><P>------------------<BR>~James<P>1986 Fiero GT! <BR>2.8 4 clicker. White face guages, blue backlighting, grey marlbe dash kit, IRM sie rocker scoops, fierostore.com 1/4 window scoop, V8 Archie Warber hood, rear added sway bar, silver mesh inserts in tail-lights, mesh inserts in turn lamp and grill, KYB shocks and struts, Eibach lowering springs, 300 watt amp, and 600 watt 12" sub, clarion pro audio 5x6" plates, Kenwood Xcelon 4x10's, clarion pro audio cd player, monster calbe wiring, rockford wiring, pheonix gold wiring, chrome ocelot exhaust tips||||reg||1
Z||000028||Fiero*101||09-09-2001||01:13 AM||||Im sooooo relieved.<BR>the poping noise was my engine wasnt getting any AIR<BR>my Filter was sooooooo bad it was rusted Shut!<P>THANK GOD!!!!<P>Fiero*101||||reg||1
